  "translation": "Good morning, Mrs. Ionescu. Please take a seat. What brings you here today? Good morning, Doctor. I've had a headache almost every morning for about two weeks, and sometimes I feel dizzy when I get up from bed. Have you measured your blood pressure at home? Yes, I have a device from my daughter. Yesterday morning I had 160 with 95. It's quite high. I'll measure it now. Please stay still for a few seconds. Okay. Please know that I also have palpitations in the evening, especially after drinking coffee. Now you have 155 with 92. How many coffees do you drink a day? Three, sometimes four. And I sleep quite poorly, about five hours a night. Please reduce your coffee to at most one a day, in the morning. Also reduce your salt as much as possible. I understand. Do you need to take any pills? Yes. I'll prescribe you amlodipine 5 milligrams, one tablet in the morning. Here's the prescription now. And for how long will you take it? For now, I'll continue. I want you to measure your blood pressure at home twice a day, in the morning and in the evening, and note the values in a notebook. Okay, I'll note them all. I'll also give you a referral for blood tests: cholesterol, blood sugar, creatinine, and electrolyte panel. Please do them by Wednesday, without fail. Can I do them at the lab next to the outpatient clinic? Yes, they have a contract with the insurance company. And I want an electrocardiogram, we'll do it right here, with the assistant, after the consultation. Perfect. When should I come back? Please come back on Friday, November 13th, at 10 o'clock, with the blood pressure notebook and the results of the tests. Noted. If the headache is very strong in the meantime? If your blood pressure goes above 180 or you have numbness, blurred vision, or chest pain, call 122 immediately. I understand. Thank you very much, Doctor. You're welcome. The assistant Maria will schedule your electrocardiogram and give you the printed prescription."
